{"task_id": "HumanEval/56", "solution": "def correct_bracketing(brackets: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return True if every opening '<' has a corresponding closing '>'.\n\n    The function processes the string left to right, keeping a counter\n    for unmatched opening brackets. For each character:\n\n    * If the character is '<', increment the counter.\n    * If the character is '>', decrement the counter.\n      If the counter would go below zero, there is an unmatched closing\n      bracket and the string is not balanced.\n\n    After processing all characters, the string is balanced only if the\n    counter is zero.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    brackets : str\n        A string consisting only of '<' and '>' characters.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    bool\n        True if the brackets are correctly balanced, False otherwise.\n\n    Examples\n    --------\n    >>> correct_bracketing(\"<\")\n    False\n    >>> correct_bracketing(\"<>\")\n    True\n    >>> correct_bracketing(\"<<><>>\")\n    True\n    >>> correct_bracketing(\"><<>\")\n    False\n    \"\"\"\n    balance = 0\n    for char in brackets:\n        if char == \"<\":\n            balance += 1\n        elif char == \">\":\n            balance -= 1\n            if balance < 0:\n                return False\n        else:\n            # If an unexpected character appears, consider the input invalid\n            return False\n    return balance == 0"}
